#heading(level: 2)[#text("Why the standard exists: the honest sentence")] <why>
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("The threat model comes first, because every mechanism in the standard is derived from it (§3). ")#strong[#text("The adversary is the operator.")]#text(" The party that produced the package is assumed to have administrative control of the machine it was produced on, and can therefore rewrite the system's records, its auxiliary state, the exported files, the manifest and the producing binaries — recomputing every digest inside the package correctly and consistently (§3.1 MA-10). Nothing inside a package proves anything against that party acting coherently; the standard calls this not a defect to be designed away but the residual every mechanism is measured against (§3.2 MA-11).")]
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("So the standard states its own residual, and every conforming validator MUST print the following two sentences verbatim on every run ")#emph[#text("that names a package")]#text(" — including a run that reports the package conformant, and including a run that ends at exit code 2 because the package could not be read (§3.3 MA-12):")]
#residual-block[#block(above: 0.45em, below: 0.45em)[#text("A package proves that what it contains was not altered after it left; it cannot prove that what it contains is all there was, and against an operator who rewrote everything before the first anchor it proves nothing.")]#block(above: 0.45em, below: 0.45em)[#text("A coherent tamper performed before the first observation is invisible to every mechanism in this standard.")]]
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("That is the whole position. A format that names its adversary can be argued with; a format that does not cannot (§3). MEASURED on this tree: the reference validator prints both sentences, word for word, in a ")#ic("residual")#text(" block on every run that names a package — ")#link(<verify>)[#text("the usage page pastes the block from a real run")]#text(" (usage.html#verify)")#text(".")]
#block(width: 100%, above: 2.2em, below: 0pt, height: 0pt, stroke: (top: 0.5pt + rule))[]
#heading(level: 2)[#text("The five mechanisms, and exactly what each buys")] <mechanisms>
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("Each mechanism is specified and reported separately, because their powers differ by orders of magnitude and a reader will otherwise credit the weakest with the strength of the strongest (§3.4). This is the standard's own table:")]
#block(width: 100%, above: 1.1em, below: 0.35em)[#text(size: 9.2pt, fill: muted)[#text("The five mechanisms, each with its exact power (§3.4)")]]
#block(width: 100%, above: 0.4em, below: 1.1em)[#table(
  columns: (auto, 1fr, 1fr, 1fr), align: left + horizon, inset: (x: 6pt, y: 4.5pt),
  stroke: (x, y) => (bottom: 0.5pt + rule),
  table.header([#strong[#text("#")]], [#strong[#text("Mechanism")]], [#strong[#text("What it buys")]], [#strong[#text("What it does not")]]), [#text("i")], [#text("Internal consistency (§5.1–5.2, §6.2, §7.1–7.2)")], [#text("A partial or sloppy rewrite shows as a break: a moved body digest at a fixed position, a gap, a count that disagrees with the payload.")], [#text("A wholesale, internally consistent rewrite passes.")], [#text("ii")], [#text("Staleness against the previous package (§7.4)")], [#text("Converts an invisible omission into a break visible one package later — if someone kept the earlier package.")], [#text("An operator who starts a fresh chain and was watched by nobody.")], [#text("iii")], [#text("Witnesses outside the audited subject (§3.6)")], [#text("Forces the operator to rewrite ")#emph[#text("more")]#text(" places consistently.")], [#text("Stops the operator. Each extra rewrite is another place to contradict a copy someone else holds — it multiplies cost, never prevention.")], [#text("iv")], [#text("The enrollment gap (§3.5)")], [#text("Nothing. It is named so it is not hoped away.")], [#text("—")], [#text("v")], [#text("The external anchor (§9)")], [#text("Proves a digest existed at a time, held by someone other than the operator.")], [#text("Truth, completeness, or that the operator told the witness everything.")])]
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("The standard also gives the one-line reading of its own layers, which is the sentence to carry away (§7.6 MA-53):")]
#quote-block[#block(above: 0.45em, below: 0.45em)[#text("Layers 0–2 stop tampering ")#emph[#text("with a package you hold")]#text("; layer 3 bounds tampering ")#emph[#text("across packages a verifier held")]#text("; only layer 4 binds the package to a party outside the operator's reach.")]]
#block(width: measure, above: 0pt, below: 0.9em)[#text("Two consequences are stated as requirements rather than left to inference. A validator report MUST show which layers were armed, and MUST NOT let an unarmed layer read as a pass (§7, §10.4 item 6). And a chain proves order and integrity over what is ")#emph[#text("present")]#text(": it does not prove completeness — a consistently-chained prefix, and a consistently-chained subset, pass every check in layers 0 and 1 (§7.2.3 MA-45).")]
